Z||000000||THOMAS DROST||05-17-2001||11:33 AM||||I HAVE  A 85 GT 2.8  THATS WAS TRICKED OUT A LITTLE??  ANY WAY AFTER A YEAR OF TRYING EVERY ELECTRICAL, MACHANICAL, AND OR MAGIG VODOO!!  I CANT GET THE CAR TO RUN RIGHT. IT SEAMS AS THOUGH THE CRANK IS BOKEN!! ANY ONE EVER EXPERIANCE THIS...?  IT WILL START, RUN NO POWER! YOU NAME IT!! I DID IT.. I EVEN BOUGHT ANOTHER 85 THAT WAS FACTORY BUT WITH A SALVAGE TITLE FOR PARTS NOW I HAVE ABOUT 3 OF EVERTHING!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||05-17-2001||11:54 AM||||Thomas, I have seen a few instances of shifted harmonic balancers lately.  The outer ring shifts from the 'correct' position so timing the car using that timing mark is impossible.  To check it, use a new/clean drinking staw in #1 cylinder, rotate to TDC using the straw and then note the markings on the HB.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-17-2001||01:57 PM||||did you start with the basics: compression test, vacuum test?<P>are you jumpering the test connector out so the timing doesnt move while your trying to adjust it?||||reg||1
